---
kind: hwlog
ext: .hwlog
version: 1
mime: application/x-hwlog
binary: false
trigger: hardware log hwlog prototype log BOM progress
---

## Purpose

Append-only hardware prototype log. One file per project or one shared yard log. Built for phone voice-to-text updates that later map to Hardware-Prototype-Tracker issues.

## Structure

1. First line is the magic banner `# hwlog v1`
2. Required YAML frontmatter between `---` fences with at least PROJECT
3. Body is append-only entries
4. An entry starts with a line `ENTRY: <integer>`
5. Following lines until the next ENTRY or EOF are `KEY: value`
6. Allowed keys: STATUS, PROGRESS, PART, BOM, SOURCE, BLOCKER, NEXT, NOTE, RIG, SEQ
7. STATUS values: Concept, Design, Prototyping, Testing, Production Ready, Complete, On Hold
8. PROGRESS is an integer 0-100
9. SEQ is a monotone integer; do not reuse

## Parse rules

- Reject the file if line 1 is not `# hwlog v1`
- Require frontmatter key PROJECT
- Split each non-comment body line on the first `: `
- Group lines under the most recent ENTRY
- Duplicate keys inside one ENTRY append; do not overwrite
- Unknown keys are kept as notes, not dropped
- Do not parse clocks. If a date-like token appears, store it raw under NOTE

## Write rules

- Always start with `# hwlog v1`
- Append only; never rewrite prior ENTRY blocks
- Next ENTRY integer is max(existing)+1
- One KEY per line
- Phone dictation maps: project name to PROJECT, percent to PROGRESS, parts to PART or BOM, stuck items to BLOCKER, upcoming work to NEXT

## Example

See examples/sample.hwlog
